cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper for the part you used. The
  preferred citation below is the 4D-STEM reconstruction paper; work using the
  core-loss STEM-EELS simulation or elastic PRISM should cite the BiP-PRISM
  paper instead, listed under references.
title: "scatterem"
version: 0.4.1
abstract: >-
  Direct (single-side-band) ptychography, tilt-corrected dark-field imaging, and
  their SSNR-weighted Wiener fusion for 4D-STEM data; and forward simulation of
  core-loss STEM-EELS by transition-potential multislice and by PRISM, including
  the bi-partitioned BiP-PRISM algorithm that partitions both the probe-forming
  and the detector scattering matrix; and elastic PRISM simulation of 4D-STEM
  with plane-wave and beam-partitioned scattering matrices.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/scatterem/scatterem"

# Authors of this software. The paper's full author list is under
# preferred-citation below.
